.TH CRS\-REMOTE 1 "2026-06-12" "Mu2e DAQ" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
crs\-remote \- run control room operations on the DAQ hosts over ssh
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B crs\-remote
.IR start | stop | status | install | provision
.RB [ \-\-session
.IR NAME ]
.RB [ \-\-host
.IR H ]
.RB [ \-\-all ]
.RB [ \-\-config
.IR FILE ]
.RB [ \-\-ssh\-config
.IR FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B crs\-remote
executes the server-side control room scripts on the DAQ hosts as the
session-owner accounts, routed through the gateway
.RB ( ProxyJump )
with Kerberos authentication.
Output lines are prefixed with
.IR [account@host] .
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B start
Run
.B start\-vnc\-session.sh
for each selected session: starts the TigerVNC server
.RB ( "\-localhost yes" ,
XFCE via xstartup) and its discovery responder sidecar.
.TP
.B stop
Run
.BR stop\-vnc\-session.sh :
kills the responder, then the VNC server.
.TP
.B status
Run
.BR status\-vnc\-session.sh ;
prints parseable
.I name|display|port|state|responder
lines.
Defaults to
.B \-\-all
when no target is given.
.TP
.B install
Ship the server payload (scripts, configs, xstartup) as a tar stream
over ssh and run
.B install\-controlroom.sh
on the host: creates
.BR ~/controlroom/{bin,etc,log} ,
adds the PATH stanza to
.BR ~/.bash_profile ,
and symlinks app start/stop scripts into the bin area.
Runs once per (host, account) pair.
.TP
.B provision
Run
.B crs\-provision\-desktop
on the host to (re)generate the XFCE desktop icons for the selected
session(s).
.SH OPTIONS
See
.BR crs\-tunnel (1)
for
.BR \-\-session / \-\-host / \-\-all / \-\-config / \-\-ssh\-config .
.SH EXAMPLES
First-time setup of one host, then everything:
.EX
    crs\-remote install \-\-session daq\-dl2
    crs\-remote start   \-\-session daq\-dl2
    crs\-remote install \-\-all
    crs\-remote start   \-\-all
    crs\-remote status
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR crs\-tunnel (1),
.BR crs\-gui (1),
.BR start\-vnc\-session (1),
.BR install\-controlroom (1)
